+
+All 1,747 PR rows are still strings of the 0.7.1 interface; none was dropped. The rows after the
+`DesignCraft 0.7.1` comment in `ko.rs` are the new ones.
+
+### Coverage
+
+The reference catalog is measured as in [localization-parity.md](localization-parity.md): every
+catalog's keys, every engine command label and menu path, the UI command labels, the menu
+titles and labels, the tool names and every literal passed to `tr`/`tr_context` in the UI crate.
+For 0.7.1 that is **1,775 strings**; Korean has **1,763 (99.3%)**. The 12 without a row stay
+English on purpose: field captions that are the same in Korean InDesign (`W:`, `H:`, `X:`,
+`Y:`), glyph captions (`IT`, `VA`, `×`) and test-only strings (`A custom name`, `Custom caption`,
+`Something new`, `Unknown label`, `Low Quality Print`). Korean covers every string the Japanese
+table covers (all 1,643 rows of `ja.rs`; enforced by a test).
+
+## Terminology
+
+Korean InDesign's terms, as Korean users know them. Menus and buttons are short nouns or noun
+phrases (저장, 새 문서…, 창에 페이지 맞추기); messages are 합니다체 (…없습니다, …선택하십시오,
+…저장하시겠습니까?).
+
+| English | Korean | Note |
+|---|---|---|
+| Text Frame | 텍스트 프레임 | |
+| Graphics frame | 그래픽 프레임 | no 0.7.1 string uses it yet; Graphic → 그래픽 |
+| Parent page (formerly Master page) | 상위 페이지 | InDesign 2022+ name; "마스터 페이지" in older versions |
+| Paragraph Styles | 단락 스타일 | |
+| Character Styles | 문자 스타일 | |
+| Tracking | 자간 | |
+| Leading | 행간 | |
+| Kerning | 커닝 | |
+| Text Wrap | 텍스트 감싸기 | |
+| Layers | 레이어 | |
+| Swatches | 견본 | |
+| Pages | 페이지 | |
+| Spread | 펼침면 | |
+| Export | 내보내기 | |
+| Package | 패키지 | |
+| Preflight | 프리플라이트 | |
+| Bleed | 재단 여백 | "도련" in older Korean prepress usage |
+| Slug | 슬러그 | |
+| Object (menu, styles) | 개체 | 고정된 개체 (anchored object), 개체 스타일 |
+| Window (menu) | 창 | 새 창, 창 분할 |
+| Place | 가져오기 | |
+| Type (menu) / Type Tool | 문자 / 문자 도구 | tools are "… 도구" |
+| Stroke / Fill | 획 / 칠 | |
+| Preferences | 환경 설정 | |
+
+Never translated: placeholders (`{name}`, `{}`), units (pt, mm, %), file formats and technology
+names (PDF, PDF/X-4, IDML, EPUB, CMYK, RGB, ICC, JPEG, PNG, SVG, CSV, MCP, URL), shortcuts.
+
+Counts read noun, number, counter: `count_label("ko", "errors", 3)` is "오류 3개".
+
+## UI font (Hangul)
+
+Korean doesn't depend on craft-fonts. `theme::font_definitions` picks the Hangul face for the
+interface:
+
+1. **An embedded craft-fonts face with Hangul**, when the build has one (craft-fonts `8dcdacd`
+   embeds Noto Sans CJK SC, which has all 11,172 syllables). With Korean selected it comes
+   ahead of the Japanese and Chinese faces in every family.
+2. **Otherwise, an installed face** (desktop only), looked up once per run and only when Korean
+   is selected: first the usual files in the system font folders without a font scan —
+   `malgun.ttf` (Malgun Gothic) on Windows, `AppleSDGothicNeo.ttc` on macOS — then by family
+   through the font database: Malgun Gothic, Apple SD Gothic Neo, Noto Sans CJK KR, Noto Sans
+   KR, Source Han Sans K, Source Han Sans KR, NanumGothic, Noto Sans CJK SC, Noto Sans CJK JP,
+   Source Han Sans SC, Gulim, Dotum. A face counts only if it has Hangul; the choice is logged.
+
+**Windows:** a release built with the craft-fonts pin `abb83316` (BIZ UD Gothic/Mincho and
+Shippori only, no Hangul) draws the Korean UI with **Malgun Gothic Regular** from
+`%WINDIR%\Fonts\malgun.ttf` (face 0), which every Windows since Vista has, Korean or not. A
+build with craft-fonts `8dcdacd` or later uses the embedded **Noto Sans CJK SC** instead and
+reads no system font. No font files were added to this repository.
+
+## System locale
+
+`i18n::language_for_locale` maps a locale to an interface language; `i18n::system_language`
+reads the system's. `ko`, `ko-KR`, `ko_KR`, `ko_KR.UTF-8` (any case, encoding or modifier) are
+Korean. The other interface languages map the same way (`ja_JP.UTF-8` → ja, `pt_BR` → pt-br,
+`zh_CN` → zh); English, unsupported languages and Traditional Chinese (`zh_TW`, `zh-Hant`) stay
+English. Sources: Windows — the user's `LocaleName` (Settings › Time & language › Region,
+`HKCU\Control Panel\International`, read with `reg.exe`, no console window), then the variables
+below; elsewhere — the first set of `LC_ALL`, `LC_MESSAGES`, `LANG` (POSIX order). The app applies
+it only when there is no saved `ui.json` (and never with `DESIGNCRAFT_NO_PREFS`), so a language
+chosen in Edit › Interface Language is kept.
+
